  "description": "A parametric LIGHT PANEL on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nDROP IT ON A NODE. It is the generic flat area source: the 600 × 600 office panel, the mirror halo, the soft fill that stands in for a window. Anything whose shadow is soft because the emitter is big.\n\nTHE THREE MOUNTINGS DIFFER IN ONE NUMBER — where the top of the body sits. Recessed puts the face on the ceiling line and the body above it; Surface hangs the whole depth below; Suspended hangs the drop as well. Everything else reads `_topZ` and none of it knows which mounting it is.\n\nAPERTURE, NOT BODY, IS WHAT MATTERS. 3600 lm behind 0.34 m² of opal is a soft light; the same 3600 lm behind a 40 mm slot is a glare source. `apertureLuminance` is that ratio and it is the number to look at before the lumens.\n\nIT DOES NOT LIGHT ANYTHING. The lamp block carries output, colour temperature, dim level and the soft-shadow radius to the renderer, and `lamp` names the Photometry file with the rest. Nothing here computes falloff.\n\nDIMENSIONS AT THE DEFAULTS: 600 × 600 × 50 mm recessed at 2.7 m, a 570 × 570 aperture, 3600 lm at 4000 K — about 3530 cd/m².",
